Z||000000||dennis_6||10-20-2001||07:41 AM||||What other vehicles would have the correct engine for an 84 4cyl Fiero.  I need a direct bolt in with very little to no modification.  The timing gear went on my brothers 84 4banger auto and he can't afford a rebuild, and if there is plastic in the engine that is gonna wear the engine down we might as well replace the engine.  Thanks.||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-20-2001||08:03 AM||||I am not 100 % sure, but I believe this is not a terminal breakage.  When you replace the timing gear be sure to get the fibre one. You should be good to go.<BR>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||dennis_6||10-20-2001||08:25 AM||||From what I heard was that the plastic gets sucked through the engine and drasticaly shortens the engines life.  The actual breakage is fixable is fixable, but the long term results are not supposed to be pleasent.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||10-20-2001||09:05 AM||||I've had 3 sets of timing gears let go over the years on my 84.  After the third time, I took the engine apart to rebuild it.  It had about 210,000 miles on it, so I figured it was due! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I did find a lot of old timing gear material in the bottom of the oil pan, some in the oil pump, some in the oil filter, and no trace of any in the bearings or any of the oil passages.  There was no scoring on the crank journals at all.<BR>I guess my point is that I don't think I'd worry too much about accelerated engine wear based on my experiance.  I did replace the gears with all metal ones the last time, so hopefully they'll last forever. I had been averaging about 65,000 miles to a set before.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||10-20-2001||10:01 AM||||<BR>Dennis, If you are up to the job of swapping engs, but little cash available,(it's that way here at my house), Drop the cradle & fix the timing gear. You can clean out most of the gear remains from the pan, replace the oil pump and check things out while you have the pan off. Cheaper than an engine swap and not quite as much work.<BR>don||||reg||1
Z||000005||dennis_6||10-20-2001||10:31 AM||||Thanks, but the engine was not very good anyways.  It needs a rebuild so my brother really need another engine.||||reg||1
